=== [2026-10-05T20:08:57Z] STAGE: code review
Independent read-only review by a separate agent (reported 8 findings; reviewer reproduced #1, #2 and #6 with scripts). Fixes:
1 HIGH  evaluation crashed on field-subset runs (GT rows for unselected fields hit report.field()). Reproduced first with new test test_field_subset_run_ignores_targets_of_unselected_fields (failed with KeyError), then fixed validate_targets (reject_unknown_fields flag; evaluation skips unselected fields).
2 MED   a second Ctrl-C during pool.shutdown released the writer lock while workers still wrote checkpoints. Added runner.drain() that re-waits through KeyboardInterrupt; test_drain_survives_repeated_interrupts.
3 MED   resume code check ignored untracked files (all of src/ was untracked) and treated commit=None as equal. Now compares source_sha256 over all package .py files; unknown hash is rejected; git diff hash now includes untracked file contents. New tests.
4 MED   httpx ReadError/RemoteProtocolError and unexpected exceptions were marked "not processed". Now outcome_unknown=True (cost becomes lower_bound); only ConnectError/ConnectTimeout/HTTP errors are "not sent". Tests extended.
5 LOW   docs claimed Ctrl-C wait is bounded by timeout_s; corrected (Gemini: upload + file processing + generation).
6 LOW   redaction missed python-repr quoted headers; regex now allows quotes around separator; 3 new cases.
7 LOW   status/evaluate lock probe could make a starting writer fail and created run.lock; probe now uses a shared lock on an existing file only, writer retries ~1 s. New test.
8 LOW   run_store docstring listed a never-written "abandoned" outcome (removed); executed_calls now counts calls actually attempted. New test.

